---
import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";

const page = getAboutPage("accounts-and-dashboard")!;
---
<AboutArticle slug={page.slug} title={page.title} description={page.description}>
  <p>
    Creating an account unlocks personalization, saved history, and optional subscription features.
    The dashboard sidebar groups tools so you can adjust the home page, manage feeds, review logs,
    and—when permitted—administer users or contact submissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Account creation and groups</h2>
  <p>
    Registration uses email and password via Supabase Auth. New users are automatically added to the
    default <code>user</code> group. Administrators belong to a separate <code>admin</code> group with
    access to user management and contact form review. Stripe subscribers join the <code>member</code> group
    for CSV export privileges.
  </p>

  <h2>Display preferences</h2>
  <p>
    Choose whether the home page shows garage temperatures, weather, or both. Preferences live in your
    user profile metadata and apply immediately after saving—no redeploy required.
  </p>

  <h2>Temperature feed configuration</h2>
  <p>
    Add HTTPS JSON feeds, name them, enable or disable individually, and map probe keys to friendly labels.
    Multiple feeds appear as grouped cards on the home page. Misconfigured URLs surface fetch errors inline
    so you can fix typos quickly.
  </p>

  <h2>Reading history and CSV export</h2>
  <p>
    Paginated history lists every snapshot stored for your account. Browsing is included for all signed-in
    users; downloading the full CSV requires an active subscription or admin access. Subscribe from the
    history page when export is locked.
  </p>

  <h2>Admin-only tools</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>User manager</strong> — review accounts and grant or revoke admin membership.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact submissions</strong> — read messages from the public contact form and export CSV.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/register">Create an account</a>,
    configure feeds under <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/temperature">Temperature settings</a>,
    load the <a class="text-link" href="/">home page</a> while signed in to begin saving history, and visit
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/history">Reading history</a> to confirm snapshots appear.
  </p>
</AboutArticle>
